    <string name="app_name">Snoozemo</string>

    <!--
      Phase 1 debug screen only. This copy is scaffolding for a device check, not
      product copy: it is replaced by onboarding and settings in later phases and
      never reaches a release, so it is deliberately not translated and has not
      been through the propose-copy-in-chat step.
    -->
    <!--
      The setup rows: a title, how the capability stands, and a button carrying
      the verb — but only while there is something left to do. A row whose
      capability is in place says so and offers nothing.

      Each action is a verb the user wants, not the route the tap takes. The old
      copy named the mechanism — `Opens Settings`, `Tap to allow`, `Tap to add`
      — which reads as a description of what is about to happen rather than an
      offer, and left a granted row still looking like it wanted something.
      `Grant` and `Allow` keep the one distinction worth carrying: Do Not
      Disturb access is a Settings toggle the user goes and flips (SPEC.md
      §5.2), while `POST_NOTIFICATIONS` is a runtime prompt that appears in
      place.
    -->
